# Lock batch and PowerShell scripts to CRLF so that cmd.exe / PowerShell
# (especially on a RU Windows that parses them in CP866) always parses
# multi-line `if (...)` blocks and `for %%x in (...) do (...)` loops correctly.
#
# Reason: MSYS-style tools (this repo's write_file path, etc.) default to LF.
# `cmd.exe` tolerates LF on simple line-based scripts but breaks on
# parenthesised blocks — the classic "Ошибка в синтаксисе команды".

*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.ps1    text eol=crlf

# Everything else follows git's normal core.autocrlf behaviour.
# (Do NOT force eol=lf on Markdown — some renderers dislike CRLF mid-table.)
